\title{\textbf{SMS Terms and Conditions}}
\author{Chargie LLC}
\date{Effective Date: May 15, 2024}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

Please read these Terms and Conditions carefully. By participating in the Chargie LLC SMS Safety and Compliance Campaign, you agree to the following terms:

\section*{1. Program Description}
The Chargie LLC SMS program is designed to deliver safety training links, compliance reminders, and operational safety alerts to field technicians and drivers.

\section*{2. Message Frequency}
Message frequency varies based on the volume of training modules assigned. Technicians can expect approximately 1--4 messages per month depending on compliance status.

\section*{3. Message and Data Rates}
Standard message and data rates may apply. Chargie LLC is not responsible for any fees charged by your mobile carrier.

\section*{4. Opt-Out (STOP)}
To stop receiving SMS messages from Chargie LLC, reply "STOP" to any message. You will receive a final confirmation message. After this, you will no longer receive SMS reminders until you re-enroll.

\section*{5. Help (HELP)}
For more information or assistance, reply "HELP" to any message or contact support directly.

\section*{6. Supported Carriers}
Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.

\section*{7. Termination}
Chargie LLC reserves the right to terminate this SMS service at any time without notice.

